KZ3 patch 2147 (RSX pass 137): descriptor-ring wrap counts in the [perf-flush] line. No behaviour change.

With RSX_PERF=1 the per-second [perf-flush] line (patch 2045) ends with
  | wraps srv S smp M up U vtx V cb C pscb P
Every wrap of a transient ring submits the list and waits for the whole queue, so U/V/C/P are the upring/vring/cbring/pscbring
flush counts of the period and the descriptor-ring flushes are split by the ring that forced them: srv = the SRV table ring was
full, smp = only the sampler ring was full. The line is built by gcm_perf_flush_line (host test tools/smoke/test_gcm_r137.sh).
Counted only when RSX_PERF is on (rsx_perf_walk_on); nothing is added to the draw path otherwise.


